{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This guide covers the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"server-side primitives"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for building authentication in TanStack Start: session cookies, session lookup, OAuth, password-reset hardening, CSRF, and rate limiting. It pairs with the "},{"type":"link","href":"/router/latest/docs/framework/react/guide/authenticated-routes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"routing-side guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"_authenticated"},{"type":"text","value":" layout, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":", redirects, RBAC)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you can use a managed solution like "},{"type":"link","href":"https://go.clerk.com/wOwHtuJ","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clerk"}]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"link","href":"https://workos.com/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"WorkOS"}]},{"type":"text","value":", prefer that — they handle most of what this guide describes. Read on if you're rolling your own."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"protect-data-first","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Protect Data First"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Authentication has a data/API boundary and a route/UI layer. The data boundary is the security boundary: every server function, server route, or API endpoint that reads or writes private data must authorize the request before returning data or mutating state."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Data/API boundary"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (this guide): issue and verify session cookies, exchange OAuth codes, hash and verify passwords, rate-limit credential endpoints, defeat user enumeration, and authorize private data access."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Route/UI layer"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"router-core/auth-and-guards"},{"type":"text","value":"): redirect unauthenticated users away from screens they cannot use, gate UI on roles/permissions, surface a login form, and avoid triggering requests that would fail anyway."}]}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A route guard is not a data authorization boundary."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Server functions and server routes are API endpoints; they are reachable independently of the route that calls them. Auth must be enforced in the handler or middleware for the endpoint that touches private data. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":" is for route UX."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"session-cookies","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Session Cookies"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default session storage is an HTTP-only cookie. The cookie can hold:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"opaque session ID"}]},{"type":"text","value":" that the server looks up in a database (recommended — easy to revoke)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"signed/encrypted token"}]},{"type":"text","value":" that carries the session payload itself (stateless, but revocation is harder)."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whichever you choose, the cookie flags matter:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/server/session.ts\nimport {\n  getRequestHeader,\n  setResponseHeader,\n} from '@tanstack/react-start/server'\n\nconst SESSION_COOKIE = '__Host-session'\nconst ONE_DAY = 60 * 60 * 24\n\nexport function setSessionCookie(token: string) {\n  setResponseHeader(\n    'Set-Cookie',\n    [\n      `${SESSION_COOKIE}=${token}`,\n      `HttpOnly`,\n      `Secure`,\n      `SameSite=Lax`,\n      `Path=/`,\n      `Max-Age=${ONE_DAY}`,\n    ].join('; '),\n  )\n}\n\nexport function clearSessionCookie() {\n  setResponseHeader(\n    'Set-Cookie',\n    `${SESSION_COOKIE}=; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Lax; Path=/; Max-Age=0`,\n  )\n}\n\nexport function readSessionToken(): string | null {\n  const header = getRequestHeader('cookie')\n  if (!header) return null\n  for (const part of header.split(/;\\s*/)) {\n    // Split only on the FIRST '=' — signed/base64 values often contain '='.\n    const eq = part.indexOf('=')\n    if (eq === -1) continue\n    if (part.slice(0, eq) === SESSION_COOKIE) return part.slice(eq + 1)\n  }\n  return null\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Flag"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HttpOnly"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JavaScript can't read the cookie. An XSS bug can't exfiltrate the session."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Secure"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"HTTPS only. Required when using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"__Host-"},{"type":"text","value":" prefix."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SameSite=Lax"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sent on top-level navigations; blocks most cross-site CSRF on POST. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Strict"},{"type":"text","value":" for higher-risk apps where loss of cross-site GET navigation is acceptable."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"__Host-"},{"type":"text","value":" prefix"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Binds the cookie to the exact origin. No "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Domain"},{"type":"text","value":" attribute, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Path=/"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Secure"},{"type":"text","value":" required. Defeats subdomain-takeover session fixation."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Path=/"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"__Host-"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Max-Age"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bounded lifetime. Pair with server-side rotation."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"session-lookup-as-middleware","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Session Lookup as Middleware"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Centralize session loading in middleware so every protected handler sees a typed session:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/server/auth-middleware.ts\nimport { createMiddleware } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { readSessionToken } from './session'\n\nexport const authMiddleware = createMiddleware({ type: 'function' }).server(\n  async ({ next }) => {\n    const token = readSessionToken()\n    const session = token ? await db.sessions.findValid(token) : null\n    if (!session) throw new Error('Unauthorized')\n    return next({ context: { session } })\n  },\n)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attach to every protected server function:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { authMiddleware } from '~/server/auth-middleware'\n\nexport const getMyOrders = createServerFn({ method: 'GET' })\n  .middleware([authMiddleware])\n  .handler(async ({ context }) => {\n    return db.orders.findMany({ where: { userId: context.session.userId } })\n  })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"login","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Login"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/server/login.functions.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\nimport { setSessionCookie } from './session'\n\nexport const login = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .validator(z.object({ email: z.string().email(), password: z.string() }))\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    const user = await db.users.findByEmail(data.email)\n    // Always run verifyPasswordHash — even when the user doesn't exist —\n    // so the user-not-found branch takes the same time as wrong-password.\n    // DUMMY_PASSWORD_HASH is a hash of any throwaway password computed once\n    // at startup with the same algorithm/cost as real password hashes.\n    const hashToCheck = user?.passwordHash ?? DUMMY_PASSWORD_HASH\n    const passwordMatches = await verifyPasswordHash(hashToCheck, data.password)\n    const ok = user != null && passwordMatches\n    if (!ok) throw new Error('Invalid email or password')\n\n    // Rotate: destroy any existing session, then issue fresh.\n    await db.sessions.revokeAllForUser(user.id)\n    const token = await db.sessions.create({ userId: user.id })\n    setSessionCookie(token)\n    return { ok: true }\n  })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Invalid email or password"},{"type":"text","value":" message is identical for \"user not found\" and \"wrong password\". The dummy-hash technique above also makes the timing identical: without it, the no-user branch returns instantly while the wrong-password branch spends ~100ms on the hash compare, leaking account existence over the wire."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"logout","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Logout"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { authMiddleware } from '~/server/auth-middleware'\nimport { clearSessionCookie } from '~/server/session'\n\nexport const logout = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .middleware([authMiddleware])\n  .handler(async ({ context }) => {\n    await db.sessions.revoke(context.session.id)\n    clearSessionCookie()\n    return { ok: true }\n  })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"oauth-state-pkce","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OAuth: state + PKCE"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For OAuth authorization-code flow:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generate a one-time random "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter — prevents CSRF on the callback."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generate a PKCE "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_verifier"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_challenge"},{"type":"text","value":" pair — defends against authorization-code interception."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Store both in a short-lived signed cookie keyed to this exact attempt."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/server/oauth.functions.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { redirect } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { setResponseHeader } from '@tanstack/react-start/server'\nimport crypto from 'node:crypto'\n\nconst OAUTH_STATE_COOKIE = '__Host-oauth'\n\nfunction base64url(buf: Buffer) {\n  return buf\n    .toString('base64')\n    .replace(/=/g, '')\n    .replace(/\\+/g, '-')\n    .replace(/\\//g, '_')\n}\n\nexport const startOAuth = createServerFn({ method: 'GET' }).handler(\n  async () => {\n    const state = base64url(crypto.randomBytes(32))\n    const verifier = base64url(crypto.randomBytes(32))\n    const challenge = base64url(\n      crypto.createHash('sha256').update(verifier).digest(),\n    )\n\n    setResponseHeader(\n      'Set-Cookie',\n      `${OAUTH_STATE_COOKIE}=${signed({ state, verifier })}; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Lax; Path=/; Max-Age=600`,\n    )\n\n    throw redirect({\n      href:\n        `https://provider.example/authorize` +\n        `?response_type=code` +\n        `&client_id=${process.env.OAUTH_CLIENT_ID}` +\n        `&redirect_uri=${encodeURIComponent(process.env.OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI!)}` +\n        `&state=${state}` +\n        `&code_challenge=${challenge}` +\n        `&code_challenge_method=S256`,\n    })\n  },\n)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In the callback handler:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read the cookie, verify its signature, and extract "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":" + "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"verifier"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compare cookie-state to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":" query param. If they don't match, abort."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exchange the authorization code for an access token, sending "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_verifier"},{"type":"text","value":" along with it."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fetch the user profile, find/create the local user record, issue a session."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clear the OAuth cookie."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If any of those checks fail, the request did not originate from your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"startOAuth"},{"type":"text","value":" and must be rejected."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"password-reset-defeat-user-enumeration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Password Reset: defeat user enumeration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The reset endpoint must NOT tell the caller whether a given email is registered. Returning 200 vs 404 — or even different copy — leaks user existence to anyone who can hit the endpoint."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nexport const requestPasswordReset = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .validator(z.object({ email: z.string().email() }))\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    const user = await db.users.findByEmail(data.email)\n    if (user) {\n      const token = await db.passwordResets.issue(user.id)\n      await sendResetEmail(user.email, token)\n    }\n    // Same response, same body, regardless of existence.\n    return { ok: true }\n  })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do NOT:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return 200 if exists, 404 if not."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vary the message (\"we sent you a link\" vs \"no account found\")."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Skip the work when the user doesn't exist (timing leak — measurable from the wire)."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"csrf-for-non-get-rpcs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"CSRF for non-GET RPCs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SameSite=Lax"},{"type":"text","value":" on the session cookie blocks most cross-site CSRF for POST/PUT/DELETE. Two cases need explicit defense:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"GET-that-mutates"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — never. Use POST/PUT/DELETE for any mutation."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"POST from a sibling subdomain"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SameSite=Lax"},{"type":"text","value":" does not block this; verify the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Origin"},{"type":"text","value":" header matches your app."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createMiddleware } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { getRequest } from '@tanstack/react-start/server'\n\nexport const csrfMiddleware = createMiddleware().server(async ({ next }) => {\n  const request = getRequest()\n  if (request.method !== 'GET' && request.method !== 'HEAD') {\n    const origin = request.headers.get('origin')\n    // Compare the FULL origin (scheme + host + port) — host alone lets\n    // http://example.com pass a check meant for https://example.com.\n    if (!origin || new URL(origin).origin !== process.env.APP_ORIGIN) {\n      throw new Error('Origin check failed')\n    }\n  }\n  return next()\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attach this in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/start.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" global "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requestMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" so it runs on every non-GET request, including server routes and SSR."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"rate-limiting-auth-endpoints","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rate Limiting Auth Endpoints"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A login endpoint without rate limiting is a credential-stuffing target. Limit per IP (and per-account if you can identify the user) with a sliding window or token bucket."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createMiddleware } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { getRequest } from '@tanstack/react-start/server'\n\nfunction rateLimitMiddleware(opts: {\n  key: string\n  max: number\n  windowMs: number\n}) {\n  return createMiddleware().server(async ({ next }) => {\n    const request = getRequest()\n    const ip =\n      request.headers.get('cf-connecting-ip') ??\n      request.headers.get('x-forwarded-for')?.split(',')[0] ??\n      'unknown'\n    const allowed = await rateLimiter.consume(\n      `rl:${opts.key}:${ip}`,\n      opts.max,\n      opts.windowMs,\n    )\n    if (!allowed) throw new Error('Too many requests')\n    return next()\n  })\n}\n\nexport const login = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' }).middleware([\n  rateLimitMiddleware({ key: 'login', max: 5, windowMs: 60_000 }),\n])\n// ...","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"session-rotation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Session Rotation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whenever the user's privileges change — login, logout, password change, role grant — destroy the old session and issue a new one. This neutralizes session-fixation attacks where an attacker plants their own session ID in the victim's browser before the privilege change."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// On login: revoke any pre-login session, create fresh.\nawait db.sessions.revokeAllForUser(user.id)\nconst token = await db.sessions.create({ userId: user.id })\nsetSessionCookie(token)\n\n// On password change / role grant:\nawait db.sessions.revokeAllForUser(user.id)\nconst token = await db.sessions.create({ userId: user.id })\nsetSessionCookie(token)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"read-cookies-and-env-per-request-not-at-module-scope","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read Cookies and Env Per Request, Not at Module Scope"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Module-scope reads are wrong on two axes:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Security:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" they can be inlined into the client bundle."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Correctness on edge runtimes:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Cloudflare Workers (and others) inject env at request time. Module-level reads run before any request exists and evaluate to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" even on the server."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// ❌ Wrong\nconst SESSION_SECRET = process.env.SESSION_SECRET\nexport function signSession(payload) {\n  return sign(payload, SESSION_SECRET)\n}\n\n// ✅ Right\nexport function signSession(payload) {\n  return sign(payload, process.env.SESSION_SECRET)\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"./execution-model.md#module-level-processenv-reads","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Execution Model: Module-Level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"process.env"},{"type":"text","value":" Reads"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the full rule."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"see-also","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See Also"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./authentication-overview.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Authentication Overview"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — choosing between partner solutions, OSS libraries, and DIY."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"/router/latest/docs/framework/react/guide/authenticated-routes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Authenticated Routes (Router)"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — the routing-side guide."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./server-functions.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server Functions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — the RPC primitive that auth lives inside."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./middleware.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Middleware"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — composing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Authentication_Cheat_Sheet.html","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OWASP Cheat Sheets — Authentication"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Session_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Session Management"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross-Site_Request_Forgery_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html","children":[{"type":"text","value":"CSRF"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Set-Cookie","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MDN — Set-Cookie"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"protect-data-first","text":"Protect Data First","level":2},{"id":"session-cookies","text":"Session Cookies","level":2},{"id":"session-lookup-as-middleware","text":"Session Lookup as Middleware","level":2},{"id":"login","text":"Login","level":2},{"id":"logout","text":"Logout","level":2},{"id":"oauth-state-pkce","text":"OAuth: state + PKCE","level":2},{"id":"password-reset-defeat-user-enumeration","text":"Password Reset: defeat user enumeration","level":2},{"id":"csrf-for-non-get-rpcs","text":"CSRF for non-GET RPCs","level":2},{"id":"rate-limiting-auth-endpoints","text":"Rate Limiting Auth Endpoints","level":2},{"id":"session-rotation","text":"Session Rotation","level":2},{"id":"read-cookies-and-env-per-request-not-at-module-scope","text":"Read Cookies and Env Per Request, Not at Module Scope","level":2},{"id":"see-also","text":"See Also","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThis guide covers the **server-side primitives** for building authentication in TanStack Start: session cookies, session lookup, OAuth, password-reset hardening, CSRF, and rate limiting. It pairs with the [routing-side guide](/router/latest/docs/framework/react/guide/authenticated-routes) (`_authenticated` layout, `beforeLoad`, redirects, RBAC).\n\nIf you can use a managed solution like [Clerk](https://go.clerk.com/wOwHtuJ) or [WorkOS](https://workos.com/), prefer that — they handle most of what this guide describes. Read on if you're rolling your own.\n\n## Protect Data First\n\nAuthentication has a data/API boundary and a route/UI layer. The data boundary is the security boundary: every server function, server route, or API endpoint that reads or writes private data must authorize the request before returning data or mutating state.\n\n- **Data/API boundary** (this guide): issue and verify session cookies, exchange OAuth codes, hash and verify passwords, rate-limit credential endpoints, defeat user enumeration, and authorize private data access.\n- **Route/UI layer** (`router-core/auth-and-guards`): redirect unauthenticated users away from screens they cannot use, gate UI on roles/permissions, surface a login form, and avoid triggering requests that would fail anyway.\n\n> **A route guard is not a data authorization boundary.** Server functions and server routes are API endpoints; they are reachable independently of the route that calls them. Auth must be enforced in the handler or middleware for the endpoint that touches private data. `beforeLoad` is for route UX.\n\n## Session Cookies\n\nThe default session storage is an HTTP-only cookie. The cookie can hold:\n\n- An **opaque session ID** that the server looks up in a database (recommended — easy to revoke).\n- A **signed/encrypted token** that carries the session payload itself (stateless, but revocation is harder).\n\nWhichever you choose, the cookie flags matter:\n\n```ts\n// src/server/session.ts\nimport {\n  getRequestHeader,\n  setResponseHeader,\n} from '@tanstack/react-start/server'\n\nconst SESSION_COOKIE = '__Host-session'\nconst ONE_DAY = 60 * 60 * 24\n\nexport function setSessionCookie(token: string) {\n  setResponseHeader(\n    'Set-Cookie',\n    [\n      `${SESSION_COOKIE}=${token}`,\n      `HttpOnly`,\n      `Secure`,\n      `SameSite=Lax`,\n      `Path=/`,\n      `Max-Age=${ONE_DAY}`,\n    ].join('; '),\n  )\n}\n\nexport function clearSessionCookie() {\n  setResponseHeader(\n    'Set-Cookie',\n    `${SESSION_COOKIE}=; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Lax; Path=/; Max-Age=0`,\n  )\n}\n\nexport function readSessionToken(): string | null {\n  const header = getRequestHeader('cookie')\n  if (!header) return null\n  for (const part of header.split(/;\\s*/)) {\n    // Split only on the FIRST '=' — signed/base64 values often contain '='.\n    const eq = part.indexOf('=')\n    if (eq === -1) continue\n    if (part.slice(0, eq) === SESSION_COOKIE) return part.slice(eq + 1)\n  }\n  return null\n}\n```\n\n| Flag             | Why                                                                                                                                                          |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `HttpOnly`       | JavaScript can't read the cookie. An XSS bug can't exfiltrate the session.                                                                                   |\n| `Secure`         | HTTPS only. Required when using the `__Host-` prefix.                                                                                                        |\n| `SameSite=Lax`   | Sent on top-level navigations; blocks most cross-site CSRF on POST. Use `Strict` for higher-risk apps where loss of cross-site GET navigation is acceptable. |\n| `__Host-` prefix | Binds the cookie to the exact origin. No `Domain` attribute, `Path=/`, `Secure` required. Defeats subdomain-takeover session fixation.                       |\n| `Path=/`         | Required by `__Host-`.                                                                                                                                       |\n| `Max-Age`        | Bounded lifetime. Pair with server-side rotation.                                                                                                            |\n\n## Session Lookup as Middleware\n\nCentralize session loading in middleware so every protected handler sees a typed session:\n\n```ts\n// src/server/auth-middleware.ts\nimport { createMiddleware } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { readSessionToken } from './session'\n\nexport const authMiddleware = createMiddleware({ type: 'function' }).server(\n  async ({ next }) => {\n    const token = readSessionToken()\n    const session = token ? await db.sessions.findValid(token) : null\n    if (!session) throw new Error('Unauthorized')\n    return next({ context: { session } })\n  },\n)\n```\n\nAttach to every protected server function:\n\n```ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { authMiddleware } from '~/server/auth-middleware'\n\nexport const getMyOrders = createServerFn({ method: 'GET' })\n  .middleware([authMiddleware])\n  .handler(async ({ context }) => {\n    return db.orders.findMany({ where: { userId: context.session.userId } })\n  })\n```\n\n## Login\n\n```ts\n// src/server/login.functions.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\nimport { setSessionCookie } from './session'\n\nexport const login = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .validator(z.object({ email: z.string().email(), password: z.string() }))\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    const user = await db.users.findByEmail(data.email)\n    // Always run verifyPasswordHash — even when the user doesn't exist —\n    // so the user-not-found branch takes the same time as wrong-password.\n    // DUMMY_PASSWORD_HASH is a hash of any throwaway password computed once\n    // at startup with the same algorithm/cost as real password hashes.\n    const hashToCheck = user?.passwordHash ?? DUMMY_PASSWORD_HASH\n    const passwordMatches = await verifyPasswordHash(hashToCheck, data.password)\n    const ok = user != null && passwordMatches\n    if (!ok) throw new Error('Invalid email or password')\n\n    // Rotate: destroy any existing session, then issue fresh.\n    await db.sessions.revokeAllForUser(user.id)\n    const token = await db.sessions.create({ userId: user.id })\n    setSessionCookie(token)\n    return { ok: true }\n  })\n```\n\nThe `Invalid email or password` message is identical for \"user not found\" and \"wrong password\". The dummy-hash technique above also makes the timing identical: without it, the no-user branch returns instantly while the wrong-password branch spends ~100ms on the hash compare, leaking account existence over the wire.\n\n## Logout\n\n```ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { authMiddleware } from '~/server/auth-middleware'\nimport { clearSessionCookie } from '~/server/session'\n\nexport const logout = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .middleware([authMiddleware])\n  .handler(async ({ context }) => {\n    await db.sessions.revoke(context.session.id)\n    clearSessionCookie()\n    return { ok: true }\n  })\n```\n\n## OAuth: state + PKCE\n\nFor OAuth authorization-code flow:\n\n- Generate a one-time random `state` parameter — prevents CSRF on the callback.\n- Generate a PKCE `code_verifier`/`code_challenge` pair — defends against authorization-code interception.\n- Store both in a short-lived signed cookie keyed to this exact attempt.\n\n```ts\n// src/server/oauth.functions.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { redirect } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { setResponseHeader } from '@tanstack/react-start/server'\nimport crypto from 'node:crypto'\n\nconst OAUTH_STATE_COOKIE = '__Host-oauth'\n\nfunction base64url(buf: Buffer) {\n  return buf\n    .toString('base64')\n    .replace(/=/g, '')\n    .replace(/\\+/g, '-')\n    .replace(/\\//g, '_')\n}\n\nexport const startOAuth = createServerFn({ method: 'GET' }).handler(\n  async () => {\n    const state = base64url(crypto.randomBytes(32))\n    const verifier = base64url(crypto.randomBytes(32))\n    const challenge = base64url(\n      crypto.createHash('sha256').update(verifier).digest(),\n    )\n\n    setResponseHeader(\n      'Set-Cookie',\n      `${OAUTH_STATE_COOKIE}=${signed({ state, verifier })}; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Lax; Path=/; Max-Age=600`,\n    )\n\n    throw redirect({\n      href:\n        `https://provider.example/authorize` +\n        `?response_type=code` +\n        `&client_id=${process.env.OAUTH_CLIENT_ID}` +\n        `&redirect_uri=${encodeURIComponent(process.env.OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI!)}` +\n        `&state=${state}` +\n        `&code_challenge=${challenge}` +\n        `&code_challenge_method=S256`,\n    })\n  },\n)\n```\n\nIn the callback handler:\n\n1. Read the cookie, verify its signature, and extract `state` + `verifier`.\n2. Compare cookie-state to the `state` query param. If they don't match, abort.\n3. Exchange the authorization code for an access token, sending `code_verifier` along with it.\n4. Fetch the user profile, find/create the local user record, issue a session.\n5. Clear the OAuth cookie.\n\nIf any of those checks fail, the request did not originate from your `startOAuth` and must be rejected.\n\n## Password Reset: defeat user enumeration\n\nThe reset endpoint must NOT tell the caller whether a given email is registered. Returning 200 vs 404 — or even different copy — leaks user existence to anyone who can hit the endpoint.\n\n```ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nexport const requestPasswordReset = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .validator(z.object({ email: z.string().email() }))\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    const user = await db.users.findByEmail(data.email)\n    if (user) {\n      const token = await db.passwordResets.issue(user.id)\n      await sendResetEmail(user.email, token)\n    }\n    // Same response, same body, regardless of existence.\n    return { ok: true }\n  })\n```\n\nDo NOT:\n\n- Return 200 if exists, 404 if not.\n- Vary the message (\"we sent you a link\" vs \"no account found\").\n- Skip the work when the user doesn't exist (timing leak — measurable from the wire).\n\n## CSRF for non-GET RPCs\n\n`SameSite=Lax` on the session cookie blocks most cross-site CSRF for POST/PUT/DELETE. Two cases need explicit defense:\n\n1. **GET-that-mutates** — never. Use POST/PUT/DELETE for any mutation.\n2. **POST from a sibling subdomain** — `SameSite=Lax` does not block this; verify the `Origin` header matches your app.\n\n```ts\nimport { createMiddleware } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { getRequest } from '@tanstack/react-start/server'\n\nexport const csrfMiddleware = createMiddleware().server(async ({ next }) => {\n  const request = getRequest()\n  if (request.method !== 'GET' && request.method !== 'HEAD') {\n    const origin = request.headers.get('origin')\n    // Compare the FULL origin (scheme + host + port) — host alone lets\n    // http://example.com pass a check meant for https://example.com.\n    if (!origin || new URL(origin).origin !== process.env.APP_ORIGIN) {\n      throw new Error('Origin check failed')\n    }\n  }\n  return next()\n})\n```\n\nAttach this in `src/start.ts` global `requestMiddleware` so it runs on every non-GET request, including server routes and SSR.\n\n## Rate Limiting Auth Endpoints\n\nA login endpoint without rate limiting is a credential-stuffing target. Limit per IP (and per-account if you can identify the user) with a sliding window or token bucket.\n\n```ts\nimport { createMiddleware } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { getRequest } from '@tanstack/react-start/server'\n\nfunction rateLimitMiddleware(opts: {\n  key: string\n  max: number\n  windowMs: number\n}) {\n  return createMiddleware().server(async ({ next }) => {\n    const request = getRequest()\n    const ip =\n      request.headers.get('cf-connecting-ip') ??\n      request.headers.get('x-forwarded-for')?.split(',')[0] ??\n      'unknown'\n    const allowed = await rateLimiter.consume(\n      `rl:${opts.key}:${ip}`,\n      opts.max,\n      opts.windowMs,\n    )\n    if (!allowed) throw new Error('Too many requests')\n    return next()\n  })\n}\n\nexport const login = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' }).middleware([\n  rateLimitMiddleware({ key: 'login', max: 5, windowMs: 60_000 }),\n])\n// ...\n```\n\n## Session Rotation\n\nWhenever the user's privileges change — login, logout, password change, role grant — destroy the old session and issue a new one. This neutralizes session-fixation attacks where an attacker plants their own session ID in the victim's browser before the privilege change.\n\n```ts\n// On login: revoke any pre-login session, create fresh.\nawait db.sessions.revokeAllForUser(user.id)\nconst token = await db.sessions.create({ userId: user.id })\nsetSessionCookie(token)\n\n// On password change / role grant:\nawait db.sessions.revokeAllForUser(user.id)\nconst token = await db.sessions.create({ userId: user.id })\nsetSessionCookie(token)\n```\n\n## Read Cookies and Env Per Request, Not at Module Scope\n\nModule-scope reads are wrong on two axes:\n\n- **Security:** they can be inlined into the client bundle.\n- **Correctness on edge runtimes:** Cloudflare Workers (and others) inject env at request time. Module-level reads run before any request exists and evaluate to `undefined` even on the server.\n\n```ts\n// ❌ Wrong\nconst SESSION_SECRET = process.env.SESSION_SECRET\nexport function signSession(payload) {\n  return sign(payload, SESSION_SECRET)\n}\n\n// ✅ Right\nexport function signSession(payload) {\n  return sign(payload, process.env.SESSION_SECRET)\n}\n```\n\nSee [Execution Model: Module-Level `process.env` Reads](./execution-model.md#module-level-processenv-reads) for the full rule.\n\n## See Also\n\n- [Authentication Overview](./authentication-overview.md) — choosing between partner solutions, OSS libraries, and DIY.\n- [Authenticated Routes (Router)](/router/latest/docs/framework/react/guide/authenticated-routes) — the routing-side guide.\n- [Server Functions](./server-functions.md) — the RPC primitive that auth lives inside.\n- [Middleware](./middleware.md) — composing `authMiddleware`.\n- [OWASP Cheat Sheets — Authentication](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Authentication_Cheat_Sheet.html), [Session Management](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Session_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html), [CSRF](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross-Site_Request_Forgery_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html).\n- [MDN — Set-Cookie](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Set-Cookie).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: authentication-server-primitives\ntitle: Authentication Server Primitives\n---\n\nThis guide covers the **server-side primitives** for building authentication in TanStack Start: session cookies, session lookup, OAuth, password-reset hardening, CSRF, and rate limiting. It pairs with the [routing-side guide](/router/latest/docs/framework/react/guide/authenticated-routes) (`_authenticated` layout, `beforeLoad`, redirects, RBAC).\n\nIf you can use a managed solution like [Clerk](https://go.clerk.com/wOwHtuJ) or [WorkOS](https://workos.com/), prefer that — they handle most of what this guide describes. Read on if you're rolling your own.\n\n## Protect Data First\n\nAuthentication has a data/API boundary and a route/UI layer. The data boundary is the security boundary: every server function, server route, or API endpoint that reads or writes private data must authorize the request before returning data or mutating state.\n\n- **Data/API boundary** (this guide): issue and verify session cookies, exchange OAuth codes, hash and verify passwords, rate-limit credential endpoints, defeat user enumeration, and authorize private data access.\n- **Route/UI layer** (`router-core/auth-and-guards`): redirect unauthenticated users away from screens they cannot use, gate UI on roles/permissions, surface a login form, and avoid triggering requests that would fail anyway.\n\n> **A route guard is not a data authorization boundary.** Server functions and server routes are API endpoints; they are reachable independently of the route that calls them. Auth must be enforced in the handler or middleware for the endpoint that touches private data. `beforeLoad` is for route UX.\n\n## Session Cookies\n\nThe default session storage is an HTTP-only cookie. The cookie can hold:\n\n- An **opaque session ID** that the server looks up in a database (recommended — easy to revoke).\n- A **signed/encrypted token** that carries the session payload itself (stateless, but revocation is harder).\n\nWhichever you choose, the cookie flags matter:\n\n```ts\n// src/server/session.ts\nimport {\n  getRequestHeader,\n  setResponseHeader,\n} from '@tanstack/react-start/server'\n\nconst SESSION_COOKIE = '__Host-session'\nconst ONE_DAY = 60 * 60 * 24\n\nexport function setSessionCookie(token: string) {\n  setResponseHeader(\n    'Set-Cookie',\n    [\n      `${SESSION_COOKIE}=${token}`,\n      `HttpOnly`,\n      `Secure`,\n      `SameSite=Lax`,\n      `Path=/`,\n      `Max-Age=${ONE_DAY}`,\n    ].join('; '),\n  )\n}\n\nexport function clearSessionCookie() {\n  setResponseHeader(\n    'Set-Cookie',\n    `${SESSION_COOKIE}=; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Lax; Path=/; Max-Age=0`,\n  )\n}\n\nexport function readSessionToken(): string | null {\n  const header = getRequestHeader('cookie')\n  if (!header) return null\n  for (const part of header.split(/;\\s*/)) {\n    // Split only on the FIRST '=' — signed/base64 values often contain '='.\n    const eq = part.indexOf('=')\n    if (eq === -1) continue\n    if (part.slice(0, eq) === SESSION_COOKIE) return part.slice(eq + 1)\n  }\n  return null\n}\n```\n\n| Flag             | Why                                                                                                                                                          |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `HttpOnly`       | JavaScript can't read the cookie. An XSS bug can't exfiltrate the session.                                                                                   |\n| `Secure`         | HTTPS only. Required when using the `__Host-` prefix.                                                                                                        |\n| `SameSite=Lax`   | Sent on top-level navigations; blocks most cross-site CSRF on POST. Use `Strict` for higher-risk apps where loss of cross-site GET navigation is acceptable. |\n| `__Host-` prefix | Binds the cookie to the exact origin. No `Domain` attribute, `Path=/`, `Secure` required. Defeats subdomain-takeover session fixation.                       |\n| `Path=/`         | Required by `__Host-`.                                                                                                                                       |\n| `Max-Age`        | Bounded lifetime. Pair with server-side rotation.                                                                                                            |\n\n## Session Lookup as Middleware\n\nCentralize session loading in middleware so every protected handler sees a typed session:\n\n```ts\n// src/server/auth-middleware.ts\nimport { createMiddleware } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { readSessionToken } from './session'\n\nexport const authMiddleware = createMiddleware({ type: 'function' }).server(\n  async ({ next }) => {\n    const token = readSessionToken()\n    const session = token ? await db.sessions.findValid(token) : null\n    if (!session) throw new Error('Unauthorized')\n    return next({ context: { session } })\n  },\n)\n```\n\nAttach to every protected server function:\n\n```ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { authMiddleware } from '~/server/auth-middleware'\n\nexport const getMyOrders = createServerFn({ method: 'GET' })\n  .middleware([authMiddleware])\n  .handler(async ({ context }) => {\n    return db.orders.findMany({ where: { userId: context.session.userId } })\n  })\n```\n\n## Login\n\n```ts\n// src/server/login.functions.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\nimport { setSessionCookie } from './session'\n\nexport const login = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .validator(z.object({ email: z.string().email(), password: z.string() }))\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    const user = await db.users.findByEmail(data.email)\n    // Always run verifyPasswordHash — even when the user doesn't exist —\n    // so the user-not-found branch takes the same time as wrong-password.\n    // DUMMY_PASSWORD_HASH is a hash of any throwaway password computed once\n    // at startup with the same algorithm/cost as real password hashes.\n    const hashToCheck = user?.passwordHash ?? DUMMY_PASSWORD_HASH\n    const passwordMatches = await verifyPasswordHash(hashToCheck, data.password)\n    const ok = user != null && passwordMatches\n    if (!ok) throw new Error('Invalid email or password')\n\n    // Rotate: destroy any existing session, then issue fresh.\n    await db.sessions.revokeAllForUser(user.id)\n    const token = await db.sessions.create({ userId: user.id })\n    setSessionCookie(token)\n    return { ok: true }\n  })\n```\n\nThe `Invalid email or password` message is identical for \"user not found\" and \"wrong password\". The dummy-hash technique above also makes the timing identical: without it, the no-user branch returns instantly while the wrong-password branch spends ~100ms on the hash compare, leaking account existence over the wire.\n\n## Logout\n\n```ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { authMiddleware } from '~/server/auth-middleware'\nimport { clearSessionCookie } from '~/server/session'\n\nexport const logout = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .middleware([authMiddleware])\n  .handler(async ({ context }) => {\n    await db.sessions.revoke(context.session.id)\n    clearSessionCookie()\n    return { ok: true }\n  })\n```\n\n## OAuth: state + PKCE\n\nFor OAuth authorization-code flow:\n\n- Generate a one-time random `state` parameter — prevents CSRF on the callback.\n- Generate a PKCE `code_verifier`/`code_challenge` pair — defends against authorization-code interception.\n- Store both in a short-lived signed cookie keyed to this exact attempt.\n\n```ts\n// src/server/oauth.functions.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { redirect } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { setResponseHeader } from '@tanstack/react-start/server'\nimport crypto from 'node:crypto'\n\nconst OAUTH_STATE_COOKIE = '__Host-oauth'\n\nfunction base64url(buf: Buffer) {\n  return buf\n    .toString('base64')\n    .replace(/=/g, '')\n    .replace(/\\+/g, '-')\n    .replace(/\\//g, '_')\n}\n\nexport const startOAuth = createServerFn({ method: 'GET' }).handler(\n  async () => {\n    const state = base64url(crypto.randomBytes(32))\n    const verifier = base64url(crypto.randomBytes(32))\n    const challenge = base64url(\n      crypto.createHash('sha256').update(verifier).digest(),\n    )\n\n    setResponseHeader(\n      'Set-Cookie',\n      `${OAUTH_STATE_COOKIE}=${signed({ state, verifier })}; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Lax; Path=/; Max-Age=600`,\n    )\n\n    throw redirect({\n      href:\n        `https://provider.example/authorize` +\n        `?response_type=code` +\n        `&client_id=${process.env.OAUTH_CLIENT_ID}` +\n        `&redirect_uri=${encodeURIComponent(process.env.OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI!)}` +\n        `&state=${state}` +\n        `&code_challenge=${challenge}` +\n        `&code_challenge_method=S256`,\n    })\n  },\n)\n```\n\nIn the callback handler:\n\n1. Read the cookie, verify its signature, and extract `state` + `verifier`.\n2. Compare cookie-state to the `state` query param. If they don't match, abort.\n3. Exchange the authorization code for an access token, sending `code_verifier` along with it.\n4. Fetch the user profile, find/create the local user record, issue a session.\n5. Clear the OAuth cookie.\n\nIf any of those checks fail, the request did not originate from your `startOAuth` and must be rejected.\n\n## Password Reset: defeat user enumeration\n\nThe reset endpoint must NOT tell the caller whether a given email is registered. Returning 200 vs 404 — or even different copy — leaks user existence to anyone who can hit the endpoint.\n\n```ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nexport const requestPasswordReset = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .validator(z.object({ email: z.string().email() }))\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    const user = await db.users.findByEmail(data.email)\n    if (user) {\n      const token = await db.passwordResets.issue(user.id)\n      await sendResetEmail(user.email, token)\n    }\n    // Same response, same body, regardless of existence.\n    return { ok: true }\n  })\n```\n\nDo NOT:\n\n- Return 200 if exists, 404 if not.\n- Vary the message (\"we sent you a link\" vs \"no account found\").\n- Skip the work when the user doesn't exist (timing leak — measurable from the wire).\n\n## CSRF for non-GET RPCs\n\n`SameSite=Lax` on the session cookie blocks most cross-site CSRF for POST/PUT/DELETE. Two cases need explicit defense:\n\n1. **GET-that-mutates** — never. Use POST/PUT/DELETE for any mutation.\n2. **POST from a sibling subdomain** — `SameSite=Lax` does not block this; verify the `Origin` header matches your app.\n\n```ts\nimport { createMiddleware } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { getRequest } from '@tanstack/react-start/server'\n\nexport const csrfMiddleware = createMiddleware().server(async ({ next }) => {\n  const request = getRequest()\n  if (request.method !== 'GET' && request.method !== 'HEAD') {\n    const origin = request.headers.get('origin')\n    // Compare the FULL origin (scheme + host + port) — host alone lets\n    // http://example.com pass a check meant for https://example.com.\n    if (!origin || new URL(origin).origin !== process.env.APP_ORIGIN) {\n      throw new Error('Origin check failed')\n    }\n  }\n  return next()\n})\n```\n\nAttach this in `src/start.ts` global `requestMiddleware` so it runs on every non-GET request, including server routes and SSR.\n\n## Rate Limiting Auth Endpoints\n\nA login endpoint without rate limiting is a credential-stuffing target. Limit per IP (and per-account if you can identify the user) with a sliding window or token bucket.\n\n```ts\nimport { createMiddleware } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { getRequest } from '@tanstack/react-start/server'\n\nfunction rateLimitMiddleware(opts: {\n  key: string\n  max: number\n  windowMs: number\n}) {\n  return createMiddleware().server(async ({ next }) => {\n    const request = getRequest()\n    const ip =\n      request.headers.get('cf-connecting-ip') ??\n      request.headers.get('x-forwarded-for')?.split(',')[0] ??\n      'unknown'\n    const allowed = await rateLimiter.consume(\n      `rl:${opts.key}:${ip}`,\n      opts.max,\n      opts.windowMs,\n    )\n    if (!allowed) throw new Error('Too many requests')\n    return next()\n  })\n}\n\nexport const login = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' }).middleware([\n  rateLimitMiddleware({ key: 'login', max: 5, windowMs: 60_000 }),\n])\n// ...\n```\n\n## Session Rotation\n\nWhenever the user's privileges change — login, logout, password change, role grant — destroy the old session and issue a new one. This neutralizes session-fixation attacks where an attacker plants their own session ID in the victim's browser before the privilege change.\n\n```ts\n// On login: revoke any pre-login session, create fresh.\nawait db.sessions.revokeAllForUser(user.id)\nconst token = await db.sessions.create({ userId: user.id })\nsetSessionCookie(token)\n\n// On password change / role grant:\nawait db.sessions.revokeAllForUser(user.id)\nconst token = await db.sessions.create({ userId: user.id })\nsetSessionCookie(token)\n```\n\n## Read Cookies and Env Per Request, Not at Module Scope\n\nModule-scope reads are wrong on two axes:\n\n- **Security:** they can be inlined into the client bundle.\n- **Correctness on edge runtimes:** Cloudflare Workers (and others) inject env at request time. Module-level reads run before any request exists and evaluate to `undefined` even on the server.\n\n```ts\n// ❌ Wrong\nconst SESSION_SECRET = process.env.SESSION_SECRET\nexport function signSession(payload) {\n  return sign(payload, SESSION_SECRET)\n}\n\n// ✅ Right\nexport function signSession(payload) {\n  return sign(payload, process.env.SESSION_SECRET)\n}\n```\n\nSee [Execution Model: Module-Level `process.env` Reads](./execution-model.md#module-level-processenv-reads) for the full rule.\n\n## See Also\n\n- [Authentication Overview](./authentication-overview.md) — choosing between partner solutions, OSS libraries, and DIY.\n- [Authenticated Routes (Router)](/router/latest/docs/framework/react/guide/authenticated-routes) — the routing-side guide.\n- [Server Functions](./server-functions.md) — the RPC primitive that auth lives inside.\n- [Middleware](./middleware.md) — composing `authMiddleware`.\n- [OWASP Cheat Sheets — Authentication](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Authentication_Cheat_Sheet.html), [Session Management](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Session_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html), [CSRF](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross-Site_Request_Forgery_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html).\n- [MDN — Set-Cookie](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Set-Cookie).\n"}
